---
const installationUrl = new URL("/guides/installation/", Astro.site).toString();
const configurationUrl = new URL(
  "/reference/configuration/",
  Astro.site,
).toString();
const releasesUrl = "https://github.com/dollarlint/dollarlint/releases/latest";

const instructions = `Install DollarLint, add project config, validate the repository, tune noisy behavior, and summarize only the remaining real findings.

## 1. Install the CLI

Pick the first method that fits the environment.

1. Homebrew available:

       brew install --cask dollarlint/tap/dollarlint

2. npm available and lifecycle scripts are allowed:

       npm install -g dollarlint

3. Go available:

       go install github.com/dollarlint/dollarlint/cmd/dollarlint@latest

   Ensure $(go env GOPATH)/bin is on PATH.

4. Otherwise, download a release archive from:

       ${releasesUrl}

   Verify checksums when practical, and put dollarlint on PATH.

Verify the install:

    dollarlint version

## 2. Create or update config

Work from the repository root.

Do not run interactive dollarlint init.

If .dollarlint.toml already exists, read it and preserve intentional settings. If none exists, write this starter and then edit it for the repo:

    version = 1

    [configs]
    mode = "single"

    [discovery]
    exclude = []
    useDefaultExcludes = true
    respectGitIgnore = true

    [schemas]
    requireCoverage = false

    [schemas.catalogs]
    enabled = true
    failure = "warn"
    match = "auto"

    [output]
    branchErrors = "best"

You may use dollarlint init --defaults to generate the full starter, but direct config edits are usually clearer.

## 3. Test and iterate

1. Run:

       dollarlint validate . --locations --show-skipped

2. If important first-party files are skipped, add [[schemas.associations]] entries or add in-file schema declarations.

3. Exclude generated files, dependency folders, snapshots, baselines, and intentionally invalid fixtures with narrow discovery.exclude patterns.

4. Use [[ignore]] only for known accepted validation issues. Do not hide unknown failures with broad excludes or ignores.

5. Re-run until discovered, validated, skipped, warning, and issue counts look reasonable for this repository.

## 4. Report to the user

Include:

- the installer chosen and dollarlint version output
- the config file created or changed
- the final validation command and summary counts
- remaining active findings grouped by file with line/column when available
- which findings were ignored or excluded and why

Separate parse errors, schema-fetch warnings, and coverage gaps from user-actionable validation findings. Do not summarize skipped files as failures.

Human docs:

- Installation: ${installationUrl}
- Configuration: ${configurationUrl}
`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Token-light DollarLint setup instructions."
    />
    <title>DollarLint install</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>DollarLint install</h1>
      <pre><code>{instructions}</code></pre>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
